ChatMeet – Privacy Policy

Last Updated: November 9, 2026

1. Introduction

Welcome to ChatMeet.

ChatMeet respects your privacy and is committed to protecting your information. This Privacy Policy explains how information is handled when you use our application.

By using ChatMeet, you agree to the practices described in this Privacy Policy.

2. Anonymity and No Login Required

ChatMeet allows users to connect and chat with strangers without creating an account or providing login credentials.

No registration or login is required.
Users are not required to provide their real names, email addresses, or phone numbers.
Users can communicate without publicly revealing their identity.
Technical information may still be processed to maintain application functionality and security.

Using ChatMeet without registration does not guarantee complete anonymity.

3. Information We Collect or Process

ChatMeet does not require users to submit personal registration information.

We do not intentionally collect users' real names, email addresses, or phone numbers.

However, certain technical information may be processed by the application or its infrastructure providers to maintain functionality, including device information, app version, technical identifiers, and network information.

4. Chat Messages and Data Storage

ChatMeet provides real-time communication between matched users.

Chat messages are transmitted between matched users for real-time communication.
We do not intentionally store or save chat messages on our servers, Firebase databases, or any other database.
We do not maintain a permanent chat history.
Chat messages are not intentionally written to persistent storage by ChatMeet.
Once a conversation ends, ChatMeet does not retain a stored conversation history.

Messages may remain temporarily visible on users' devices during an active conversation.

5. Media Sharing

ChatMeet does not currently provide image uploading or image storage functionality.

We do not operate an image-hosting service for user-uploaded content through the application.

6. Third-Party Services

ChatMeet uses Google Firebase for necessary application infrastructure and technical functionality.

Firebase services may process technical information required to provide these services.

ChatMeet does not use Firebase to store or save users' chat messages.

7. Analytics and Tracking

ChatMeet does not currently use dedicated analytics services to track user behavior.

We do not intentionally track individual users' conversations or maintain chat histories.

Technical information may still be processed by infrastructure providers as necessary for service operation.

8. Data Sharing

We do not sell users' personal information.

ChatMeet does not intentionally store or share chat message histories.

Information may be processed by service providers to maintain application functionality and security, or disclosed to authorities when legally required.

9. Data Security

We take reasonable measures to protect information processed through ChatMeet.

However, no internet-based service can guarantee absolute security.

Users should avoid sharing sensitive personal information, passwords, financial information, phone numbers, or home addresses with strangers.

10. Data Retention and Deletion

ChatMeet does not intentionally maintain stored chat histories or persistent chat message records.

Since users are not required to create accounts, there are no traditional user accounts to delete.

Certain technical information may be processed or retained by infrastructure providers according to their applicable service policies.

11. Adults-Only Platform (18+)

ChatMeet is exclusively intended for adults aged 18 years and above.

Individuals under 18 are strictly prohibited from using the application.
We do not knowingly permit minors to access ChatMeet.
If we become aware that a minor is using the platform, we will take appropriate action to restrict access.
Users are encouraged to report suspected underage users and child safety violations.

Please also review our Child Sexual Abuse and Exploitation (CSAE) Policy.

12. User Safety

Users are responsible for their interactions with other people on ChatMeet.

We strictly prohibit harassment, bullying, hate speech, illegal activities, child exploitation, and abusive behavior.

Users should report inappropriate behavior through the available reporting mechanism.

13. Children's Privacy

ChatMeet is not intended for children or individuals under the age of 18.

We do not knowingly permit minors to use the application. If we become aware that a minor has accessed ChatMeet, we will take appropriate steps to restrict access in accordance with applicable laws.

14. Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our application, services, or legal requirements.

Updates will be published on this page with a revised Last Updated date.

